{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.PagedSpectralSequence","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.page_stabilises_of_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.page_stabilises_of_parity","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L135-L152","doc":"**The payoff, chained.** A parity-graded spectral sequence stabilises: from\npage `r₀` on, the next page is isomorphic to this one.\n\nThis is the statement the substrate axiom `S-GB-spectral-collapse` wants,\nnow reachable from a grading rather than posited. Supplying the grading for\nthe Gröbner filtration is the remaining work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.collapses_of_parity_mismatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.collapses_of_parity_mismatch","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L112-L133","doc":"**Collapse, proved from the grading.**\n\nA `PagedSS` carrying a bar involution on every page, whose differentials\nare equivariant and run purely-even → purely-odd from page `r₀` on,\ncollapses at `r₀`.\n\nNothing is assumed about the filtration; the grading does the work. Compare\n`GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2`, which asserted the conclusion and was\ndischarged by a `PUnit` model — see\n`SpectralSequence.collapse_is_definitional`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.map_eq_zero_of_parity_mismatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.map_eq_zero_of_parity_mismatch","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L91-L110","doc":"**A parity-mismatched equivariant map is zero.**\n\nIf `f` intertwines the two involutions, the source is purely even and the\ntarget purely odd, then every `f x` is both even (transported from the\nsource) and odd (by the target's grading) — hence zero.\n\nThis is `ZBarParity`'s exclusion applied to a map rather than a scalar, and\nit is what makes a grading force a differential to vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.eq_zero_of_even_and_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.eq_zero_of_even_and_odd","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L76-L89","doc":"**Even and odd meet only at zero** — the module form of\n`ZBarParity.bar_even_and_odd_two_mul_eq_zero`.\n\n2-torsion-freeness is a hypothesis rather than a field assumption, so this\nis usable over `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` and not only after specialising to `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.IsOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.IsOdd","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L73-L74","doc":"`x` is bar-**odd**: negated by the involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.IsEven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.IsEven","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L70-L71","doc":"`x` is bar-**even**: fixed by the involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.bar_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.bar_bar","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L66-L66","doc":"It squares to the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.bar","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse.BarInvolution","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BarGradedCollapse.lean#L59-L66","doc":"A **bar involution** on an `R`-module: an `R`-linear map squaring to the\nidentity. The fibre involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` of `ZBarParity` induces one on\nevery module the corpus grades by it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}